WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.186
Your hazard study contains the engineering behind the plant's protection.

00:00:04.669 --> 00:00:09.053
Veriso Barrier Report turns that study into a clear, structured report,

00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:13.159
showing the hazards, the barriers and the questions your engineers need

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:13.955
to review.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.535
Start with your signed HAZOP, spreadsheet or scanned study.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.924
The converter reads the content and retains the link to the

00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:24.804
original document, row and words.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.554
Your units, roles and conventions shape the output.

00:00:29.037 --> 00:00:31.648
Uncertain material is flagged for resolution.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:36.447
Hazard screening identifies the major-accident scenarios that need bow ties.

00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:41.427
Causes, the central event and consequences become a visible structure, with

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:44.458
prevention and mitigation barriers on the relevant paths.

00:00:45.034 --> 00:00:48.980
Other deviations remain in the register, keeping the picture focused.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.221
The report brings together five outputs in your own format: bow

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:57.528
ties, a barrier register, a candidate list of safety-critical

00:00:57.548 --> 00:01:02.068
equipment, gaps for engineering review, and HAZOP worksheets.

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:05.284
Each connects back to the same model, so the team can

00:01:05.304 --> 00:01:09.916
move between a diagram, a barrier and its source without rebuilding

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.770
the picture.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.636
Engineers review the interpretation, confirm proposed criticality and

00:01:15.656 --> 00:01:17.889
decide which equipment is safety-critical.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.300
They can trace the assumptions, resolve questions and sign the resulting

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.507
snapshot. That gives the plant a coherent study record to discuss,

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.248
hand over and use as the basis for further engineering work.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.969
The worksheets also support the next study.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.439
For a new plant, reference templates can help prepare a first

00:01:36.459 --> 00:01:40.120
draft. The study team still examines the hazards and makes the

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.806
decisions, starting with organised information rather than an empty page.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:48.028
Barrier Report gives you the structured study snapshot.

00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:52.149
The full Process and Barrier solution carries that model into ongoing

00:01:52.169 --> 00:01:55.528
management of impairments, changes and checks.

00:01:56.221 --> 00:02:00.892
Two connected offers, with a clear starting point: understand the protection

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:02.233
your study describes.
